      "explanation": "(1)\n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/eKCUJHpd6pFrwMsLh/5oM0r2ac6FGiQ3bHGRewi37cBfkFZ/WsOPh4XPlHnXjYU8rENWFF/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Offline) Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 167 English Explanation 1\">\n<br><br>Here oxygen(O) has lone so it will attach on H<sup>+</sup> of HI and H<sup>+</sup> will attach with O atom to form oxonium ion.\n<br><br>(2) \n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/65315BYjtXWNPSPVg/m9m42jc6II2kvlxjwVa1hlORmc6B9/RxlzZWv5S4Mtctbu5F5qz1/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Offline) Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 167 English Explanation 2\">\n<br><br>As O is more electronegative atom, so it don't want to hold the positive charge so it will break bond to create 2<sup>o</sup> cation which is stable.\n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/JC8ZpdtMIkNfTR8G8/5shXhyArhjtkJ2AKXSpMda1uyO2bD/KeUxjMZbamhjIDtQf0jvGv/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Offline) Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 167 English Explanation 3\">\n<br><br>Now with this cation I<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup>  ion is added. \n<br><br>(3) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.133ex\" height=\"0.036ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" view